Interactive controls (round 13): a manipulate value shows its result at the initial positions; moving a control
keeps its position on the output and shows the result there. The fake kernel answers a control's evaluation with
its source, so the scripts show what the kernel was asked.

=== a manipulate value asks for its result at the initial positions
--- before
#% cell
manipulate(a+1, [a, 0, 10, 1], [[b, 2], 0, 1])▮
--- keys
Shift+Enter
--- after
#% cell label=1
manipulate(a+1, [a, 0, 10, 1], [[b, 2], 0, 1])
#% output n=1
#= manipulate(a+1, [a, 0, 10, 1], [[b, 2], 0, 1])
#% output manipulated
#= { let a = 0; let b = 1.0; a+1 }
‖

=== moving a control keeps its position and shows the new result; the file reads back the same
--- before
#% cell
manipulate(a+1, [a, 0, 10, 1])▮
--- keys
Shift+Enter Control(1,0,7) ControlDone(1,0,3)
--- after
#% cell label=1
manipulate(a+1, [a, 0, 10, 1])
#% output n=1 controls=3
#= manipulate(a+1, [a, 0, 10, 1])
#% output manipulated
#= { let a = 3; a+1 }
‖

=== a saved position is evaluated from where it was, and re-evaluating the input starts at the initial one
--- before
#% cell label=1
manipulate(a+1, [a, 0, 10, 1])▮
#% output n=1 controls=5
#= manipulate(a+1, [a, 0, 10, 1])
#% output manipulated
#= 6
--- keys
Control(1,0,6)
--- after
#% cell label=1
manipulate(a+1, [a, 0, 10, 1])▮
#% output n=1 controls=6
#= manipulate(a+1, [a, 0, 10, 1])
#% output manipulated
#= { let a = 6; a+1 }
